From: Chongbiao Chen <chenchongbiao@radxa.com>
Date: Mon, 7 Jul 2026 19:00:00 +0800
Subject: Fix frame lifecycle corruption on mode-set + hotplug

Two fixes for frame lifecycle issues that cause permanent compositor
freeze after resolution switch followed by monitor hotplug:

1. meta_frame_native_release(): replace g_return_if_fail assertion
   with g_clear_object() to gracefully release dangling KMS updates.
   During hotplug, a pending frame may be freed before its KMS update
   is submitted — this is expected, not a programming error.

2. notify_view_crtc_presented(): when frame_info is NULL (e.g. because
   the mode-set fallback callback already consumed it), still call
   notify_frame_complete / promote_posted_frame / maybe_post_next_frame
   to ensure the frame clock driver schedules the next frame.
   Previously the g_return_if_fail returned early, skipping
   maybe_post_next_frame and permanently freezing the compositor.

Bug-Radxa: freeze after resolution switch + hotplug on Q6A (SC7280)
Last-Update: 2026-07-07
---
diff --git a/src/backends/native/meta-frame-native.c b/src/backends/native/meta-frame-native.c
index 98cd917c73..0c1bcc94dd 100644
--- a/src/backends/native/meta-frame-native.c
+++ b/src/backends/native/meta-frame-native.c
@@ -48,7 +48,7 @@ meta_frame_native_release (ClutterFrame *frame)
   g_clear_object (&frame_native->buffer);
   g_clear_object (&frame_native->scanout);
 
-  g_return_if_fail (!frame_native->kms_update);
+  g_clear_object (&frame_native->kms_update);
 }
 
 MetaFrameNative *
diff --git a/src/backends/native/meta-onscreen-native.c b/src/backends/native/meta-onscreen-native.c
index 3975e36d06..f615aacc5e 100644
--- a/src/backends/native/meta-onscreen-native.c
+++ b/src/backends/native/meta-onscreen-native.c
@@ -245,7 +245,13 @@ notify_view_crtc_presented (MetaRendererView *view,
 
   frame_info = cogl_onscreen_peek_head_frame_info (onscreen);
 
-  g_return_if_fail (frame_info != NULL);
+  if (!frame_info)
+    {
+      meta_onscreen_native_notify_frame_complete (onscreen);
+      meta_onscreen_native_promote_posted_frame (onscreen);
+      maybe_post_next_frame (onscreen);
+      return;
+    }
 
   frame_counter = cogl_frame_info_get_frame_counter (frame_info);
